From e8a810e86f941079000fd26e16b44328294f319a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 09:14:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] Stop inventing publication dates

scrape-ngo-news set published_date to new Date() - the moment of scraping - so
every article it ingested claimed to have been published the instant CivilWire
found it. An NGO report from 2023 appeared dated today, and /cite rendered
formal academic citations carrying that invented date.

Read the page's own metadata instead (publishedTime, article:published_time,
datePublished and the usual variants), rejecting values before 1995 or more
than a day in the future. When the page states no date, published_date stays
null: an unknown date must read as unknown, never as today.

Extracted to _shared/published-date.ts, free of Deno globals, with nine tests
covering the regression directly.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
